 1289: ### 22.6 Secrets and environment (frozen)
 1290: 
 1291: A field is a secret if `ui.type == "password"` **or** its key matches `SENSITIVE_KEYS_RE`
 1292: (`api_key|token|secret|password|auth|bearer|credential`, `settings_manager.py:214-217`).
 1293: 
 1294: - Secrets are stored in `settings/settings.json` in plaintext (unchanged; the file is
 1295:   local-only). The contract governs **egress**, not at-rest encryption.
 1296: - Secrets must never appear in an API response, log line, error message, execution record, SSE
 1297:   frame, exported template, or archive. Every settings payload leaving the process passes
 1298:   through `redact_settings` / `redacted_provider_settings`.
 1299: - **Live defect recorded here, not fixed by 10.2:** `GET /api/settings/v2`
 1300:   (`editor/routes.py:211-212`) and `GET /api/providers/<domain>/<provider_id>/settings`
 1301:   (`editor/routes.py:360-366`) return **unredacted** provider settings, including `api_key`.
 1302:   `redacted_provider_settings` exists (`settings_manager.py:247-249`) with **zero call sites**
 1303:   outside `__all__`. Owner: **11.5**, which must also decide how the modal round-trips a
 1304:   redacted value without overwriting the real one (rule: a field whose submitted value is
 1305:   exactly the redaction sentinel `"***"` is ignored on save).
 1306: - **Env vars are a read-time fallback, never a seed for secrets.** A provider resolves a
 1307:   credential as `settings[key] or os.environ[ENV_NAME]`, and the resolved value is never
 1308:   written back to `settings.json` and never returned. This replaces copying values in
 1309:   `_seed_from_env` (`settings_manager.py:85-104`). Owner: **11.3**.
