 1315: ## 23. Parameterized option sources (frozen)
 1316: 
 1317: Freezes Â§15.1. `GET /api/workflow/options/<source>` currently calls `resolve_options(source)`
 1318: with no context (`options.py:108`, `routes.py:196`), which is why `_tts_voices()` returns the
 1319: static Kokoro list regardless of engine (`options.py:19-21`) and why no `tts_providers` source
 1320: exists at all. 12.2 implements this; 15.2 depends on it.
 1321: 
 1322: ### 23.1 Request
 1323: 
 1324: ```
 1325: GET /api/workflow/options/<source>?domain=<d>&provider=<p>&node_type=<t>&project_id=<id>
 1326: ```
 1327: 
 1328: The source stays **allowlisted** â€” `<source>` must be a key of `ASYNC_OPTION_SOURCES`; a
 1329: schema-supplied URL is still never fetched (Â§11). `ASYNC_OPTION_SOURCES`
 1330: (`registry.py:30-34`) changes from a list to a dict of specs. Every existing consumer uses
 1331: `set(...)` or `in` (`options.py:75`, `tests/test_workflow_options.py:60`,
 1332: `tests/test_workflow_registry.py:81`), so the parity assert and its test survive unchanged.
 1333: 
 1334: ```python
 1335: ASYNC_OPTION_SOURCES = {
 1336:     "tts_voices": OptionSourceSpec(context=("domain", "provider"), cache="settings"),
 1337:     "tts_providers": OptionSourceSpec(context=(), cache="discovery"),      # new (P26)
 1338:     "storyboard_providers": OptionSourceSpec(context=(), cache="discovery"),
 1339:     "animator_providers": OptionSourceSpec(context=(), cache="discovery"),
 1340:     "script_providers": OptionSourceSpec(context=(), cache="discovery"),          # new
 1341:     "scene_blueprint_providers": OptionSourceSpec(context=(), cache="discovery"), # new
 1342:     "story_tones": OptionSourceSpec(context=(), cache="static"),
 1343:     "style_templates": OptionSourceSpec(context=(), cache="static"),
 1344:     "export_profiles": OptionSourceSpec(context=(), cache="static"),
 1345:     "caption_presets": OptionSourceSpec(context=(), cache="static"),
 1346: }
 1347: ```
 1348: 
 1349: **Context validation is an allowlist too.** Only the parameter names in that source's
 1350: `context` tuple are accepted; any other query parameter is ignored. `domain` must be a
 1351: `DOMAINS` key; `provider` must resolve in that domain's registry (id or alias, normalized to
 1352: the canonical id before it reaches the resolver); `node_type` must be a registry node type;
 1353: `project_id` must survive `sanitize_project_id` unchanged. A declared parameter may be
 1354: omitted â€” the resolver then falls back to the domain's selected provider (Â§24), which is what
 1355: makes existing single-argument callers keep working.
 1356: 
 1357: The five per-domain `*_providers` sources make P26 and P32 disappear: the TTS node's `engine`
 1358: field stops being a static `["kokoro","inworld"]` list (`registry.py:186`) and
 1359: `_provider_options` stops hardcoding two domains (`options.py:38-50`).
 1360: 
 1361: ### 23.2 Response
 1362: 
 1363: ```json
 1364: {
 1365:   "source": "tts_voices",
 1366:   "context": {"domain": "tts", "provider": "inworld"},
 1367:   "options": [{"value": "Ashley", "label": "Ashley", "group": null, "disabled": false}],
 1368:   "generated_at": "2026-08-08T00:00:00Z"
 1369: }
 1370: ```
 1371: 
 1372: `context` echoes the **validated, normalized** context so the client can key its cache on the
 1373: server's interpretation rather than on its own query string. `group` and `disabled` are
 1374: optional and default to `null`/`false`; `{value, label}` remains the minimum, so today's
 1375: `_opt()` helper (`options.py:15-16`) is unchanged and the existing client
 1376: (`useOptionSources.js:14`, reads `data.options`) keeps working without edits.
