 1378: ### 23.3 Failure semantics (frozen)
 1379: 
 1380: | condition | HTTP | code |
 1381: |---|---|---|
 1382: | unknown `<source>` | 404 | `NOT_FOUND` (unchanged, `routes.py:200`) |
 1383: | context parameter invalid, unknown domain/provider, or fails sanitization | 400 | `OPTION_CONTEXT_INVALID` |
 1384: | resolver raised â€” provider unreachable, model missing, extension offline | 503 | `PROVIDER_UNAVAILABLE` (unchanged, `routes.py:198`) |
 1385: 
 1386: `OPTION_CONTEXT_INVALID` is the only addition to the stable error-code list in Â§7; it is
 1387: additive and no existing code changes meaning. The 503 body carries a redacted message and
 1388: never the provider's raw exception.
 1389: 
 1390: **Save-time validation still fails open.** `allowed_option_values` (`options.py:85-105`)
 1391: becomes context-aware but keeps its contract from step 6.3: a bad value is rejected, an
 1392: unavailable resolver returns `None` and never blocks saving an otherwise-valid workflow. For
 1393: a context-sensitive source the legal set is the **union** over the currently registered
 1394: providers of that domain, so switching provider can never retroactively invalidate a saved
 1395: workflow.
