  901: v4's vocabulary is otherwise adopted unchanged: *manifest*, *capabilities*, *runtime hook*,
  902: *broken-provider isolation*, and *rich job snapshots* (already implemented as `job_meta` in
  903: `services.py`), plus *per-domain provider folders*.
  904: 
  905: ### 17.7 Out of scope — Music and Captions (confirmed working, not migrated)
  906: 
  907: Neither has a `providers/` package, a provider ID, or any dispatch branch. Music is
  908: `studio/music/selector.py` (`select_music`, `select_random_music`, `recall_last_music`) with a
  909: 10-entry history; Captions is `studio/captions/routes.py` (`_group_words_into_captions`,
  910: `CAPTION_PRESETS`). Both are consumed by the `music.select` / `captions.generate` nodes and by
  911: Assemble. They touch the provider platform at exactly two points, both of which must keep
  912: resolving: the `caption_presets` and `story_tones` option sources (`options.py:53-61` and
  913: `:24-26` — the latter reads `studio.music.selector.TONE_MUSIC_MAP`). No migration work;
  914: regression-only.
  915: 
  916: ## 18. Coverage assertion
  917: 
  918: Every path that reaches a model or provider was enumerated: five domains × {legacy HTTP route,
  919: legacy pipeline step, workflow adapter}, plus the WebSocket transports, the internal
  920: HTTP-to-self hop, the preflight probe, the provider settings/health API, and the legacy frontend
  921: pages/settings consumers. The four
  922: never-provider-driven surfaces (frontend story templates, scene blueprint, music, captions) are
  923: explicitly accounted for. The unexecuted provider path groups (§16) and forty-seven hardcoded
  924: provider-decision entries (§15) each carry an owner step. No item in §13–§17 is left without
  925: an owner.
