  934: # Provider Contract v2 (Phase 10.2 frozen)
  935: 
  936: > Produced by step 10.2 of [implementation-plan.md](implementation-plan.md).
  937: > Grounded in code at commit `e79ac1c` (2026-08-08); §13–§18 above is the audit this
  938: > contract is built on. Every `file:line` reference was read at that commit.
  939: >
  940: > **Reuse rule.** This contract *extends* the shipped
  941: > `studio/shared/providers_common/` (registry, manifest, settings manager, discovery,
  942: > migrations, runtime hooks, broken-provider isolation). Nothing here authorizes a parallel
  943: > framework. Where v2 differs from today's code the delta is stated with an owner step, so
  944: > Phase 11 is a set of edits to existing modules, never a rewrite.
  945: >
  946: > **What 10.2 does not freeze.** Invocation context, request/result envelopes, job handles,
  947: > and `ProviderError` belong to 10.3. Legacy field/alias mapping tables and fixtures belong
  948: > to 10.4. This section stops at *what a provider is, how it is found, how it is configured,
  949: > and what the browser may see*.
  950: 
  951: ## 19. Domains, packages, identity
  952: 
  953: ### 19.1 Domain catalog — data, not code
  954: 
  955: Exactly **five** domains are supported. Music and Captions are excluded by owner decision
  956: (§17.7) and have no `DomainSpec`.
  957: 
  958: | domain id | label | provider package | discovery base | default provider | legacy selection key |
  959: |---|---|---|---|---|---|
  960: | `script` | Script / Story | `studio.story.providers` | `studio/story/providers` | `random_template` | *(none)* |
  961: | `scene_blueprint` | Scene Blueprint | `studio.build_scene_blueprints.providers` | `studio/build_scene_blueprints/providers` | `n8n_webhook` | *(none)* |
  962: | `tts` | Text to Speech | `studio.tts.providers` | `studio/tts/providers` | `kokoro` | `sts-tts-provider` |
  963: | `storyboard` | Storyboard | `studio.storyboard.providers` | `studio/storyboard/providers` | `gemini_ws` | `sts-storyboard-provider` |
  964: | `animator` | Animator | `studio.animator.providers` | `studio/animator/providers` | `grok_automa` | `sts-asset-provider` |
  965: 
  966: The catalog lives in **one** new module, `studio/shared/providers_common/domains.py`,
  967: exporting `DOMAINS: dict[str, DomainSpec]` in the declaration order above.
  968: 
  969: ```python
  970: @dataclass(frozen=True)
  971: class DomainSpec:
  972:     id: str                      # catalog key; also settings.json domains.<id>
  973:     label: str                   # human label for the provider modal
  974:     package: str                 # dotted import path of the provider package
  975:     providers_base: str          # absolute path, built with os.path.join(ROOT_DIR, ...)
  976:     default_provider: str        # last-resort selection; must exist after discovery
  977:     capability_vocabulary: frozenset[str]   # §20.4
  978:     legacy_selection_key: str | None        # app-config.json key being retired (§24)
  979:     request_model: str | None = None        # dotted path — filled by 10.3
  980:     result_model: str | None = None         # dotted path — filled by 10.3
  981: ```
  982: 
  983: Adding a sixth domain is one `DomainSpec` entry plus a provider folder. It must not require
  984: editing the registry class, the settings manager, a route, or a Vue component.
  985: 
  986: **This catalog replaces both hardcoded three-domain sets.** `ProviderRegistry.VALID_DOMAINS`
  987: (`registry.py:177`, P29) becomes `frozenset(DOMAINS)`; the duplicate `valid_domains`
  988: in `settings_manager.validate_settings` (`settings_manager.py:270`, P30) reads the same
  989: constant; `_default_settings()` (`settings_manager.py:137-160`, P31) is generated by
  990: iterating `DOMAINS` instead of listing three literals. Owner: **11.1**, in one step, so the
  991: two can never drift again. A test must assert all three derive from `DOMAINS` and that
  992: `settings.json` accepts every catalog domain.
  993: 
  994: ### 19.2 Package layout (frozen)
  995: 
  996: ```
  997: studio/<module>/providers/
  998:   __init__.py            one shared binding (§27) — not a per-domain copy
  999:   <provider_id>/
 1000:     manifest.py          REQUIRED — def manifest() -> ProviderManifest
 1001:     provider.py          optional — factory + validate_settings + health_check + impl
 1002:     settings_schema.py   optional — def settings_schema() -> dict
 1003:     __init__.py          optional; MUST NOT be required for discovery
 1004: ```
 1005: 
 1006: Discovery keys on `manifest.py` only (`registry.py:246-249`); folders starting with `_` or
 1007: `.` are skipped (`registry.py:243`). Modules are loaded from file paths under synthetic names
 1008: `_sts_provider_{domain}_{id}_{manifest|provider|schema}` (`registry.py:273`), which is why
 1009: blocker **B8** stands: consumers resolve providers with `registry.get(id)` and never `import`
 1010: a provider module. `kie_ai/__init__.py` re-exporting `get_provider` (§14.1) is the one
 1011: existing violation and is deleted by 14.3.
 1012: 
 1013: Provider folders stay owned by their module. One hub (§27) exposes all domain registries;
 1014: it does not move the folders.
 1015: 
 1016: ### 19.3 Provider identity and versions (frozen)
 1017: 
 1018: | field | rule |
 1019: |---|---|
 1020: | `id` | `^[a-z][a-z0-9_]{1,31}$`; **must equal the folder name** (already enforced, `registry.py:320-323`); unique within its domain. The registry key is the pair `(domain, id)` — the same id may exist in two domains. |
 1021: | `aliases` | **new, optional** `list[str]`, same charset as `id`. Legacy wire strings (`gemini`, `webhook`, `direct`, `grok`, `kie-ai`, `midjourney`) move here, retiring the hand-written tables at `pipeline/services.py:550`/`:644` and `animator/schemas.py:30-36` (P7, P8, P34). Resolution order: exact `id` first, then alias. An alias that collides with a real id **loses**, and the collision is logged WARN and recorded in `excluded()` metadata. Aliases are never written to settings and never returned as `selected`. The concrete mapping table is 10.4's deliverable; 10.2 freezes only the mechanism. |
 1022: | `version` | semver `MAJOR.MINOR.PATCH`, the *implementation* version. Informational: it is never used to gate compatibility, and it is carried into result provenance (10.3). |
 1023: | `contract_version` | **new, optional** `int`, default `2`. `1` = the legacy ABC shape (all seven providers today; never executed, §14.1/§16). The registry loads both; only `2` may be invoked through the 10.3 invocation contract. A value above the build's maximum excludes the provider with reason `MANIFEST_UNSUPPORTED_CONTRACT`. |
 1024: | `domain` | must equal the owning registry's domain or registration is refused (`registry.py:196-199`). |
 1025: 
 1026: Provider IDs in node configurations and `settings.json` are **canonical ids only**; legacy
 1027: strings are accepted on input and normalized through the alias table (§8, "registry ids are
 1028: canonical").
 1029: 
 1030: ## 20. Manifest contract
 1031: 
 1032: ### 20.1 Fields
 1033: 
 1034: `ProviderManifest` (`registry.py:17-27`) is the frozen carrier. Required and optional fields:
 1035: 
 1036: | field | required | type | default | notes |
 1037: |---|---|---|---|---|
 1038: | `id` | yes | str | — | §19.3 |
 1039: | `label` | yes | str | — | shown in the provider modal and every dropdown |
 1040: | `domain` | yes | str | — | must be a `DOMAINS` key |
 1041: | `kind` | yes | enum | — | `local` \| `cloud` \| `extension` \| `webhook` (§20.2) |
 1042: | `version` | yes | str | — | semver |
 1043: | `capabilities` | yes | `dict[str,bool]` | — | **must be non-empty**: `registry.py:314-318` treats a falsy value as missing, so `capabilities={}` silently excludes the provider. This trap is frozen as-is and documented in the author guide (owner 16.2). |
 1044: | `requires` | no | `list[str]` | `[]` | settings **key names** that must be non-empty for the provider to be usable (§21.5). Never values. |
 1045: | `open_url` | no | `str \| None` | `None` | URL the UI may offer to open for `extension` providers |
 1046: | `aliases` | no | `list[str]` | `[]` | new (§19.3); owner 11.2 |
 1047: | `contract_version` | no | `int` | `2` | new (§19.3); owner 11.2 |
 1048: | `description` | no | `str \| None` | `None` | new; one sentence, browser-safe |
 1049: | `docs_url` | no | `str \| None` | `None` | new; must be `http(s)` |
 1050: 
 1051: ### 20.2 `kind` semantics (frozen)
 1052: 
 1053: - `local` — runs in-process, no network (today: `kokoro`). May own heavy singletons; must
 1054:   implement `shutdown()`.
 1055: - `cloud` — outbound HTTPS to a third-party API with credentials in settings (today:
 1056:   `inworld`, `wavespeed_direct`, `kie_ai`).
 1057: - `webhook` — outbound HTTP to a user-supplied URL, validated by `is_safe_webhook_url`
 1058:   (today `wavespeed_webhook` is declared `cloud`; 14.2 reclassifies it).
 1059: - `extension` — needs a browser extension and a WebSocket runtime; the **only** kind whose
 1060:   `register_runtime(app, sock)` is called at boot (`<domain>/providers/__init__.py:47-52`)
 1061:   (today: `gemini_ws`, `grok_automa`). The two WS URLs are frozen public surface (§17.1).
 1062: 
