    docs(providers): step 10.2 - Freeze plugin, manifest, and settings contracts
    
    Extends contracts.md with Provider Contract v2 (§19-§29), built on the shipped
    studio/shared/providers_common/ rather than a parallel framework.
    
    Frozen: the five-domain catalog as data (replacing both hardcoded three-domain
    sets), package layout, provider id/alias/version rules, every required and
    optional manifest field, the kind and capability vocabularies, manifest
    validation order and unknown-field policy, the discovery -> create() -> shutdown()
    lifecycle, discovery order, duplicate-ID resolution, nine broken-plugin exclusion
    reason codes, settings-schema widgets and conditional fields, secret/env handling,
    the availability and health state machines, and the browser-safe serialization
    allowlist.
    
    The two contracts later steps are blocked on are frozen with migration paths: the
    parameterized option-source envelope (context allowlist, response shape, failure
    codes, cache invalidation) and settings.json domains.*.selected_provider as the
    single authoritative selection store. §26 shows a new provider needs no workflow
    node, route dispatcher, or Vue component edit; §28 lists all 19 code deltas with
    owner steps.

