 1161: ### 21.2 Registration and discovery order (frozen)
 1162: 
 1163: 1. Domains initialize in `DOMAINS` declaration order: `script`, `scene_blueprint`, `tts`,
 1164:    `storyboard`, `animator` — replacing the fixed three-call sequence at `app.py:90-95`.
 1165: 2. Within a domain, providers are loaded in **`sorted()` order of folder name**. Today
 1166:    `os.listdir` order is used unsorted (`registry.py:239`); sorting is required so discovery
 1167:    logs, catalog responses, and "first wins" duplicate resolution are deterministic.
 1168:    Owner: **11.1**.
 1169: 3. Discovery is idempotent — a second `discover()` on a registry that already scanned is a
 1170:    no-op (`<domain>/providers/__init__.py:20-23`). Dev reload explicitly resets the flag after
 1171:    calling `shutdown()` on constructed providers.
 1172: 4. Extension runtimes bind after **all** domains have been discovered, never interleaved with
 1173:    discovery, so a runtime can rely on the full catalog being present.
 1174: 5. Registration never touches `app.py` or `studio/workflows/registry.py`.
 1175: 6. Discovery and dev reload build a private catalog snapshot and publish it with one atomic
 1176:    swap. Concurrent requests see either the complete old snapshot or the complete new one,
 1177:    never a partially discovered catalog. Providers removed by the swap are shut down only
 1178:    after new lookups can no longer acquire them and all pre-swap invocation leases have
 1179:    drained; teardown must not close a provider still serving an old-snapshot request.
