 1349: ### 23.1 Request
 1350: 
 1351: ```
 1352: GET /api/workflow/options/<source>?domain=<d>&provider=<p>&node_type=<t>&project_id=<id>
 1353: ```
 1354: 
 1355: The source stays **allowlisted** — `<source>` must be a key of `ASYNC_OPTION_SOURCES`; a
 1356: schema-supplied URL is still never fetched (§11). `ASYNC_OPTION_SOURCES`
 1357: (`registry.py:30-34`) changes from a list to a dict of specs. Every existing consumer uses
 1358: `set(...)` or `in` (`options.py:75`, `tests/test_workflow_options.py:60`,
 1359: `tests/test_workflow_registry.py:81`), so the parity assert and its test survive unchanged.
 1360: 
 1361: ```python
 1362: ASYNC_OPTION_SOURCES = {
 1363:     "tts_voices": OptionSourceSpec(context=("domain", "provider"), cache="settings"),
 1364:     "tts_providers": OptionSourceSpec(context=(), cache="discovery"),      # new (P26)
 1365:     "storyboard_providers": OptionSourceSpec(context=(), cache="discovery"),
 1366:     "animator_providers": OptionSourceSpec(context=(), cache="discovery"),
 1367:     "script_providers": OptionSourceSpec(context=(), cache="discovery"),          # new
 1368:     "scene_blueprint_providers": OptionSourceSpec(context=(), cache="discovery"), # new
 1369:     "story_tones": OptionSourceSpec(context=(), cache="static"),
 1370:     "style_templates": OptionSourceSpec(context=(), cache="static"),
 1371:     "export_profiles": OptionSourceSpec(context=(), cache="static"),
 1372:     "caption_presets": OptionSourceSpec(context=(), cache="static"),
 1373: }
 1374: ```
 1375: 
 1376: **Context validation is an allowlist too.** Only the parameter names in that source's
 1377: `context` tuple are accepted; any other query parameter is rejected with
 1378: `OPTION_CONTEXT_INVALID` (silently ignoring a misspelling can resolve options for the global
 1379: default provider). `domain` must be a
 1380: `DOMAINS` key; `provider` must resolve in that domain's registry (id or alias, normalized to
 1381: the canonical id before it reaches the resolver); `node_type` must be a registry node type;
 1382: `project_id` must survive `sanitize_project_id` unchanged. A declared parameter may be
 1383: omitted — the resolver then falls back to the domain's selected provider (§24), which is what
 1384: makes existing single-argument callers keep working.
 1385: 
 1386: The five per-domain `*_providers` sources make P26 and P32 disappear: the TTS node's `engine`
 1387: field stops being a static `["kokoro","inworld"]` list (`registry.py:186`) and
 1388: `_provider_options` stops hardcoding two domains (`options.py:38-50`).
 1389: 
 1390: ### 23.2 Response
 1391: 
 1392: ```json
 1393: {
 1394:   "source": "tts_voices",
 1395:   "context": {"domain": "tts", "provider": "inworld"},
 1396:   "options": [{"value": "Ashley", "label": "Ashley", "group": null, "disabled": false}],
 1397:   "generated_at": "2026-08-08T00:00:00Z"
 1398: }
 1399: ```
 1400: 
 1401: `context` echoes the **validated, normalized** context so the client can key its cache on the
 1402: server's interpretation rather than on its own query string. `group` and `disabled` are
 1403: optional and default to `null`/`false`; `{value, label}` remains the minimum, so today's
 1404: `_opt()` helper (`options.py:15-16`) is unchanged and the existing client
 1405: (`useOptionSources.js:14`, reads `data.options`) keeps working without edits.
