  962: ### 11.1 Generalize the registry into a domain hub
  963: Extend `studio/shared/providers_common/registry.py` so supported domains are declared through a
  964: domain catalog rather than the current `VALID_DOMAINS` set (`registry.py:177`) — and retire the
  965: duplicate hardcoded domain set in `settings_manager.validate_settings` (`settings_manager.py:270`) in
  966: the same step, so the two can never drift. Replace the three copies of the 57-line
  967: `studio/<domain>/providers/__init__.py` (tts, storyboard, animator — structurally identical, differing
  968: only in domain name and `init_<domain>_registry`; see contracts §14.6) with one generated/shared
  969: binding. Add a process-wide registry hub that can
  970: list and resolve `(domain, provider_id)` while preserving the existing per-module `registry`,
  971: `get_provider`, and `list_providers` imports as compatibility facades. Domain registration must bind
  972: the request/result contract and provider search path once; individual provider registration must not
  973: touch `app.py` or the workflow registry.
  974: 
