  976: still work; duplicate domains/providers fail deterministically; discovery order is stable; and tests
  977: prove one broken or duplicate provider cannot hide healthy providers or stop application startup.
  978: 
  979: ### 11.2 Provider discovery, factories, and lifecycle isolation
  980: Upgrade discovery to validate the whole provider package (`manifest.py`, `provider.py`, optional
  981: `settings_schema.py` and runtime hooks) before atomic registration. Instantiate providers through a
  982: factory instead of module-level ID branching, cache only where declared, and shut down initialized
  983: instances safely. Preserve extension/WebSocket startup through `call_provider_runtime`, but drive it
  984: from manifest capabilities rather than provider IDs. Dev hot-reload swaps only a fully valid provider
  985: catalog and retains the last good version after an invalid edit.
